+# Agent Note: Initialized Session presentation
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-13-initialized-session-presentation.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+An application can initialize meaningful content before calling a model. Turn-only list visibility hides that Session, while indexing arbitrary configuration would expose strings never intended as conversation content.
+
+## Decision
+
+The session/configuration event accepts optional producer-owned presentation fields. initialized preserves list visibility without a turn; label describes the Session purpose; text explicitly contributes searchable content. These fields do not enter model requests. Existing authored-context events remain the model-history mechanism.
+
+The list projection has its own cache version. Search queries current user, assistant and authored-context events, then log-only configuration display text, retaining the existing visibility checks and combined result limit. Separate queries preserve the current-only restriction on ordinary messages. The SQLite full-text index uses derived schema 9 to rebuild semantic extraction; canonical Session data is untouched.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+A synthetic user message or model turn would misrepresent author and usage. Indexing every configuration value would include implementation details. Including every log-only message would expose shadowed or non-current content. Application-specific checks in the controller would couple the host to individual products.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Initializing plugins own their display text and must separately declare actual model input. Generic plugins without presentation keep existing list and search behavior. Validation, list, search, SDK and browser evidence cover the added fields; no Agent Loop stage or released Session generation changes.
